#: src/quiet-recipes.md:1
msgid "Quiet Recipes"
msgstr ""

#: src/quiet-recipes.md:3
msgid ""
"A recipe name may be prefixed with `@` to invert the meaning of `@` before "
"each line:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quiet-recipes.md:13
msgid "Now only the lines starting with `@` will be echoed:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quiet-recipes.md:22
msgid "All recipes in a justfile can be made quiet with `set quiet`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quiet-recipes.md:24
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set quiet\n"
"\n"
"foo:\n"
"  echo \"This is quiet\"\n"
"\n"
"@foo2:\n"
"  echo \"This is also quiet\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/quiet-recipes.md:34
msgid "The `[no-quiet]` attribute overrides this setting:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quiet-recipes.md:36
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set quiet\n"
"\n"
"foo:\n"
"  echo \"This is quiet\"\n"
"\n"
"[no-quiet]\n"
"foo2:\n"
"  echo \"This is not quiet\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/quiet-recipes.md:47
msgid "Shebang recipes are quiet by default:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quiet-recipes.md:60
msgid ""
"Adding `@` to a shebang recipe name makes `just` print the recipe before "
"executing it:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quiet-recipes.md:76
msgid ""
"`just` normally prints error messages when a recipe line fails. These error "
"messages can be suppressed using the `[no-exit-message]`<sup>1.7.0</sup> "
"attribute on individual recipes, or module-wide with `set no-exit-"
"message`<sup>1.39.0</sup>. You may find this especially useful with a recipe "
"that wraps a tool:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quiet-recipes.md:93
msgid ""
"Add the attribute to suppress the exit error message when the tool exits "
"with a non-zero code:"
msgstr ""
